  "wikitext": "{{Short description|Species of flowering plant}}\n{{Speciesbox\n| image = Spiraea prunifolia var. simpliciflora 2014년 4월 9일 (13768093393).jpg\n| image_caption = ''Spiraea prunifolia'' var. ''simpliciflora''\n| genus = Spiraea\n| species = prunifolia\n| authority = Siebold & Zucc.\n}}\n\n'''''Spiraea prunifolia''''', commonly called '''bridalwreath spirea''',<ref>{{PLANTS|id=SPPR|taxon=Spiraea prunifolia|accessdate=27 November 2015}}</ref> is a species of the genus ''[[Spiraea]]'', sometimes also spelled ''Spirea''. It flowers mid-spring, around May 5, and is native to [[Japan]], [[Korea]], [[China]], and [[Taiwan]]. It is sometimes cultivated as a garden plant elsewhere.\n\n==References==\n{{Commons category}}\n{{Reflist}}\n\n{{Taxonbar|from=Q1055383}}\n\n[[Category:Spiraea|prunifolia]]\n\n\n{{amygdaloideae-stub}}",
